{
    "pageid": 385,
    "title": "Mods",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "A mod (short for modification ) is an alteration of the game and objective of modding . There's a large variety of mods, everything from small tweaks to total conversions."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Mod creators or players may create a wiki page for their preferred mod or tool, to act as a collaborative documentation of its features."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Installation",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Mods can be downloaded and installed manually from User Modifications sub-forum ( game registration needed ), or automatically from Steam Workshop ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The mod installation folder is:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Windows: ~\\Documents\\Paradox Interactive\\Crusader Kings II\\mod\\",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Linux: ~/.paradoxinteractive/Crusader Kings II/mod/",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Mac: ~/Documents/Paradox Interactive/Crusader Kings II/mod/",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Never install mods in Steam directory (ex: C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Steam\\SteamApps\\common\\Crusader Kings II\\mod), as mod would not be properly loaded."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Check in the mod description the CK2 version compatible with the version of the mod. If needed, rollback to an older patch , using Steam Beta tab. [1]"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In case of manual installation, the steps are usually the following (refer to specific mod instructions, if any):"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ol",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Remove any existing installation of the mod (mod folder and .mod file). This is very important, as the game loads all files present in mod folder, so old mod files that are no longer present or were renamed in a new version of the mod would conflict.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Clear your gfx cache, by deleting the folder ~\\Documents\\Paradox Interactive\\Crusader Kings II\\<mod_name>\\gfx , if any.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Extract the downloaded archive, so that CK2 mod folder contains the .mod file and directory of the mod.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Launch CK2 and select the mod in the Mod tab. Note that the mod may have a different name in the launcher than the name of the .mod file.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Play!",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "For more info, see the structure of a mod ."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Mod compatibility",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Some smaller mods may be timeless, but most often a mod is only compatible with a specific vanilla patch , and players need to check the version and potentially rollback to an older patch ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Incompatibilities happens when a mod:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "has to overwrite vanilla files, usually because of modding restrictions or limits to folder-based loading behavior .",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "is a total conversion and/or major overhaul, and is deeply tied to vanilla.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In addition mods may be incompatible with each others, if they modify the same vanilla files or entities (graphic sprites, defines, ...). Refer to the mod FAQs for known incompatibilities."
                }
            ]
        },
